{"reference":"Jeremiah 3","book":"Jeremiah","chapter":3,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Jeremiah in Its Larger Book","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Jeremiah 3 belongs to a book that brings together several forms of material, including poetry, prose sermons, narratives, letters, headings, repeated accounts, restoration collections, oracles concerning nations, and an appendix. Its long compositional and textual history means that the book’s broad arrangement is useful as a practical guide, but does not by itself settle questions about how every part was composed.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_jeremiah_003_8f8ea2203e92cd936de963ff"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}